<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-7464] Add property to configure time between node connection attempts</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-7464</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Currently when a node attempts to join the cluster, the connection algorithm will be repeated until successful or timed out. The time between the attempts is hardcoded - 2 seconds.&lt;br/&gt;
It might be useful to adjust that time via a property (say, in SPI config) based on the network quality, application constraints, etc.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
